Subject: ghostnet: define ghostnetJsonField() in the no-transport build too

A build without libcurl (which is every iOS build — the SDK has none, and
PD_HAVE_CURL is off by the charter's 0.7 default) does not link:

  Undefined symbols: _ghostnetJsonField, referenced from _communityResolve

ghostnetJsonField() is defined at ghostnet.c:350, inside `#ifdef PD_GHOST_NET`,
but community.c calls it at :457/:481-483/:515 and is not guarded on anything.
Nothing has noticed because every desktop packager has libcurl installed.

The stub finds nothing, which is the honest answer when nothing can be fetched
in the first place, and matches the other stubs in that block. Worth sending
upstream — it is a real bug in a configuration upstream supports.

diff --git a/port/src/ghostnet.c b/port/src/ghostnet.c
index 1666c3210..55cbe5ccf 100644
--- a/port/src/ghostnet.c
+++ b/port/src/ghostnet.c
@@ -1878,6 +1878,24 @@ const char *ghostnetGetMessage(void)
 // would clear is only ever the idle one.
 void ghostnetClearState(void) { }
 
+/**
+ * The JSON scanner, which lives above the #else and so is not compiled here.
+ *
+ * community.c calls it to read GitHub's release JSON and is NOT itself guarded
+ * on PD_GHOST_NET, so a build with no transport does not link without this -
+ * which is why nothing has noticed: every desktop packager has libcurl. There
+ * is nothing to parse when nothing can be fetched, so it finds nothing.
+ */
+bool ghostnetJsonField(const char *json, const char *end, const char *key,
+		char *out, u32 outsize)
+{
+	if (out && outsize) {
+		out[0] = '\0';
+	}
+
+	return false;
+}
+
 /**
  * The one seam every caller goes through, answered here so that none of them
  * has to know whether a transport was built in.
